# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HealThaali — repository root
#
# The Astro website lives in ./website and is the only thing this repository
# tracks: 7.4 MB in total. Everything at this outer level is either source
# material the site is *derived* from, or local tooling state.
#
# LAUNCH.md §4 lists every ignored path with its measured size and the reason.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Outer source material / local tooling

# 44 MB and 164 files, its own node_modules included, against a 7.4 MB
# repository. It is the read-only input to `npm run assets`
# (website/scripts/extract-assets.mjs), which derives the images the site serves
# into website/src/assets/ — those are committed, because a host build needs
# them and this folder is not there.
/asset/

/.freebuff/

# Backups of this repository, made by `npm run backup`, and the scratch clone
# that `npm run backup -- --drill` restores into and builds. A bundle of the
# whole history cannot live inside the history it duplicates: it belongs in
# cloud storage, or on another machine. See RESTORE.md.
/backups/
/.restore-drill/

# 2,412 lines written for the build this site was: a working document, not
# repository documentation. What outlives it is in website/README.md.
/HealthAali_Astro_Website_Build_Guide.md

# Lighthouse reports from a manual measurement of the deployed site
# (see LAUNCH.md §6). Regenerated on demand, never worth committing.
lighthouse-*.json

# Operating system cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*~
